+# Native Rust Converter and Theme Refresh Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Replace Tauri's Node document sidecar with local in-process Rust conversion, regroup and expand built-in themes, localize all new text, and deliver one cumulative patch against `markdown-explorer-2026-07-28-005234.zip`.
+
+**Architecture:** Tauri dispatches convertible files into focused Rust adapters and returns normalized Markdown plus a stable quality code. Electron and VS Code keep `@the-long-ride/markdown-them`. The Settings picker renders one dropdown card per theme family, while CSS theme tokens/selectors keep Focus and Tabs behavior aligned.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Rust 2021/Tauri 2, `office_oxide`, `pdf-extract`, `html2markdown`, `calamine`, `rtf-parser`, `quick-xml`, `zip`, React 19, TypeScript, CSS tokens, Vitest/Testing Library, Node contract tests.
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Package manager baseline remains exactly `pnpm@11.17.0`.
+- Tauri conversion is local-only and must not spawn Node or any external converter.
+- New Rust dependencies must be MIT, Apache-2.0, or dual MIT/Apache-2.0 and must not add telemetry.
+- Electron and VS Code retain `@the-long-ride/markdown-them` behavior.
+- Existing convertible extensions remain DOC, DOCX, PDF, HTML, XLS, XLSX, XLM, PPTX, ODT, ODP, ODS, and RTF.
+- Legacy DOC/XLS/XLM conversion is best-effort and emits the stable `legacy-best-effort` warning code.
+- Theme picker renders at most Themes, Pet themes, and Your custom themes.
+- Existing `glass` persistence ID remains compatible and becomes Aurora Glass.
+- New IDs are `neon-voltage` and `raw-grid`.
+- Every new user-facing string is translated in en, vi, fr, es, zh, no, ja, ko, and ru.
+- Tests are written before corresponding production changes.
+- Final output is one cumulative binary-safe `.patch`; no generated Node runtime or other large runtime binary is committed.
