+# Native Rust Document Converter and Theme Refresh Design
+
+Date: 2026-07-28
+
+Status: Approved
+Package manager baseline: `pnpm@11.17.0`
+
+## Goals
+
+1. Replace the Tauri Node/`markdown-them` child-process sidecar with an in-process, 100% local Rust document converter.
+2. Keep Electron and VS Code on their current `@the-long-ride/markdown-them` adapters.
+3. Preserve the existing preview/cache/UI contract while improving error classification and localized quality warnings.
+4. Rework the Settings theme picker so users see at most three groups: Themes, Pet themes, and Your custom themes.
+5. Refresh selected theme layouts, replace Evolved Glass, and add two additional built-in themes.
+6. Translate every new user-facing string across all nine supported languages and cover new behavior with tests.
+7. Deliver one cumulative binary-safe patch against the uploaded `pnpm@11.17.0` source tree.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- No Node runtime, process sidecar, runtime download, network conversion, cloud API, or telemetry in Tauri.
+- No rewrite of Electron or VS Code conversion internals.
+- No promise of pixel-perfect Office/PDF rendering; output remains a Markdown preview.
+- No unrelated redesign of custom-theme creation/remixing.
+- No new file extensions beyond the extensions currently classified as convertible.
+
+## Architecture decision
+
+Use **Approach A**:
+
+- **Tauri:** native Rust conversion in-process.
+- **Electron and VS Code:** retain `@the-long-ride/markdown-them`.
+- **Chromium/web variants:** retain current browser capability boundaries.
+- **Cross-variant tests:** share fixtures and contract assertions where practical, without forcing one runtime implementation onto all variants.
+
+## Existing behavior to preserve
+
+The Tauri `DocumentConverter` remains responsible for:
+
+- extension classification;
+- Markdown/text passthrough;
+- conversion enable/disable behavior;
+- title insertion when converted output has no heading;
+- failure Markdown generation;
+- cache lookup by path, modified time, and file size;
+- preview metadata such as duration and cache status.
+
+The native converter replaces only the sidecar call boundary.
+
+## Native Rust converter design
+
+### Module layout
+
+Create a focused conversion subsystem under `tauri/src/render/native_document_converter/`:
+
+- `mod.rs`: public dispatch API, common result/error types, extension and signature routing.
+- `office.rs`: DOC, DOCX, XLS, XLSX, XLM, and PPTX.
+- `pdf.rs`: PDF text extraction and paragraph normalization.
+- `html.rs`: HTML-to-Markdown conversion.
+- `odf.rs`: ODT and ODP ZIP/XML conversion.
+- `spreadsheet.rs`: ODS table conversion and shared Markdown table utilities.
+- `rtf.rs`: RTF parsing and style-to-Markdown conversion.
+- `markdown.rs`: escaping, headings, lists, tables, whitespace, and output normalization helpers.
+
+Public API:
+
+```rust
+pub fn convert_file(path: &Path) -> Result<ConversionOutput, ConversionError>;
+```
+
+```rust
+pub struct ConversionOutput {
+    pub markdown: String,
+    pub quality: ConversionQuality,
+}
+
+pub enum ConversionQuality {
+    Standard,
+    BestEffortLegacy,
+}
+```
+
+Errors are typed internally and converted into safe, concise messages at the existing preview boundary. Raw parser diagnostics may be included in the fenced error details but must not panic the app.
+
+### Dependency selection
+
+All conversion dependencies must be permissively licensed, local-only, and configured without telemetry or JavaScript bindings.
+
+- `office_oxide` with default features disabled for DOC, DOCX, XLS, XLSX, and PPTX Markdown conversion.
+- `pdf-extract` for local PDF text extraction.
+- `html2markdown` for HTML structure conversion.
+- `calamine` for ODS workbook parsing and deterministic Markdown tables.
+- `rtf-parser` with default features disabled for RTF parsing.
+- existing/new `quick-xml` and `zip` use for focused ODT/ODP container parsing.
+
+The implementation must pin resolved versions in `Cargo.lock`. Dependency review must confirm:
+
+- no production network client is introduced by the selected feature set;
+- no telemetry SDK is present;
+- no Node, Python, JVM, C/C++ helper, external executable, or runtime download is required;
+- licenses are MIT, Apache-2.0, or dual MIT/Apache-2.0.
+
+### Format behavior
+
+#### DOCX
+
+Prefer structured Markdown from `office_oxide`: headings, paragraphs, lists, emphasis, links, and tables when exposed by the crate. Preserve document order and Unicode. Unsupported drawing/layout details are omitted rather than guessed.
+
+#### DOC
+
+Use `office_oxide` legacy parsing. Always mark successful output as `BestEffortLegacy`. Preserve text and exposed structure; do not claim layout fidelity.
+
+#### XLSX
+
+Use `office_oxide` Markdown output, retaining sheet order and table cells. Normalize empty cells and Markdown-sensitive characters deterministically.
+
+#### XLS and XLM
+
+Use the legacy XLS reader. `.xlm` is routed by file signature as legacy Excel data rather than relying on its extension. Successful output is always `BestEffortLegacy`. If the signature is unsupported, return a conversion error rather than silently treating binary data as text.
+
+#### PPTX
+
+Use `office_oxide`, preserving presentation/slide order. Each slide must have a stable Markdown boundary, with titles and body text emitted in reading order as exposed by the parser.
+
+#### PDF
+
+Use `pdf-extract` locally. Normalize extracted text into paragraphs and preserve Unicode. Scanned/image-only PDFs return the existing “no readable content” preview; OCR is out of scope.
+
+#### HTML
+
+Use `html2markdown` to preserve headings, lists, links, images, blockquotes, tables, code blocks, and inline formatting. Script/style content must not become visible Markdown.
+
+#### ODS
+
+Use `calamine` to read sheets and ranges. Emit a heading per sheet and a GitHub-style Markdown table per non-empty range. Preserve sheet order, cell values, and Unicode.
+
+#### ODT
+
+Read `content.xml` from the ZIP container using bounded extraction and `quick-xml`. Convert headings, paragraphs, lists, links, basic emphasis, tables, and explicit line breaks in document order.
+
+#### ODP
+
+Read presentation XML and relationship data using bounded extraction. Preserve slide order. Emit a heading per slide and text/list/table content in XML reading order.
+
+#### RTF
+
+Use `rtf-parser` with JavaScript bindings disabled. Convert paragraphs and available bold/italic/underline/list metadata. Guard parser invocation so malformed content becomes a conversion error rather than terminating the application. Embedded binary/image payloads are ignored safely.
+
+### Output normalization
+
+All adapters pass through shared normalization:
+
+- trim trailing whitespace;
+- collapse excessive blank lines without joining semantic blocks;
+- escape table delimiters and control characters;
+- keep existing headings;
+- let the outer `DocumentConverter` add the filename heading only when none exists;
+- produce deterministic output for cache and tests;
+- preserve Unicode and line breaks.
+
+### Cache and quality metadata
+
+Extend cached conversion entries to retain `ConversionQuality`, not only Markdown and duration. A cached legacy document must still display the legacy warning.
+
+Add a stable preview warning code while retaining the existing English fallback for bridge compatibility:
+
+```text
+converted-preview
+legacy-best-effort
+conversion-failed
+```
+
+The UI translates codes using the active language. Unknown/missing codes fall back to the existing string.
+
+### Removal work
+
+Remove all Tauri Node-sidecar pieces:
+
+- `tauri/src/render/sidecar.rs` and module export;
+- `tauri/sidecar/mdthem-sidecar/`;
+- `tauri/scripts/prepare-document-sidecar.mjs`;
+- `prepare:document-sidecar` scripts and Tauri before-build hooks;
+- `externalBin` and document-sidecar resources;
+- generated/bundled Node binaries;
+- Snap/workflow sidecar staging;
+- sidecar-specific tests and package-lock entries that become unused.
+
+Add a contract test that fails if Tauri reintroduces Node process launching, sidecar configuration, or a bundled runtime.
+
+## Theme picker design
+
+### Three-group model
+
+The appearance picker renders at most three group cards:
+
+1. **Themes** — all non-pet built-in themes in one dropdown.
+2. **Pet themes** — existing pet themes in one dropdown.
+3. **Your custom themes** — shown only when custom themes exist and the caller enables custom themes.
+
+Each group card contains:
+
+- a group swatch;
+- translated label and description;
+- current selection;
+- a keyboard-accessible listbox dropdown;
+- active styling when that group owns the active theme.
+
+Selecting a built-in or pet theme clears the active custom-theme selection through the existing state action. Selecting a custom theme activates its base style and custom ID through the existing custom-theme action. The last selected item within each group remains the default when returning to that group during the current session.
+
+Dropdown requirements:
+
+- close on outside pointer interaction and Escape;
+- correct `aria-haspopup`, `aria-expanded`, `role=listbox`, `role=option`, and `aria-selected` values;
+- translated listbox labels;
+- no hard-coded English component strings.
+
+### Built-in themes
+
+Built-in IDs and compatibility:
+
+- `default` — Default.
+- `glass` — renamed and redesigned as **Aurora Glass**; the `glass` ID remains unchanged so saved settings and custom-theme bases continue working.
+- `bento` — Bento Grids.
+- `vercel` — Vercel.
+- `tokyo-night` — Tokyo Night.
+- `neon-voltage` — **Neon Voltage**, deep-black surfaces with sunset coral, electric teal, and glowing purple accents.
+- `raw-grid` — **Raw Grid**, Cloudflare-inspired raw brutalism with visible grid structure, honest borders, asymmetric rhythm, and restrained orange accents.
+
+Update `ThemeStyle`, normalization, constants, imports, swatches, custom-theme base-style support, persistence, and tests for the two new IDs.
+
+### Aurora Glass replacement
+
+Aurora Glass replaces the visual implementation and labels of Evolved Glass while preserving `glass` as the persistence ID. It uses:
+
+- translucent layered surfaces;
+- controlled backdrop blur;
+- soft pastel gradients;
+- clearer edge contrast than the old implementation;
+- floating panels without reducing text contrast;
+- matching light, dark, and auto behavior.
+
+### Tabs header parity
+
+For Aurora Glass, Bento Grids, Vercel, and Tokyo Night, the Tabs view header must use the same visual header treatment as Focus view. Shared selectors/tokens should drive both modes; avoid duplicate one-off overrides.
+
+### Tokyo Night spacing
+
+Tokyo Night sidebar and TOC receive a small, consistent gap below the application header. The gap must not create clipping, double spacing, or broken resize handles in Focus or Tabs mode.
+
+### Raw Grid visual direction
+
+Use the supplied Cloudflare screenshot as direction, not as a pixel clone:
+
+- dark near-black canvas;
+- visible structural grid/borders;
+- square or lightly rounded geometry;
+- mechanical, asymmetric grouping;
+- orange accent used selectively;
+- high legibility and visible focus states;
+- no Cloudflare logos, trademarks, or copied text.
+
+## Localization
+
+Update translation types and all nine language entries:
+
+- English (`en`)
+- Vietnamese (`vi`)
+- French (`fr`)
+- Spanish (`es`)
+- Chinese (`zh`)
+- Norwegian (`no`)
+- Japanese (`ja`)
+- Korean (`ko`)
+- Russian (`ru`)
+
+New translated strings include:
+
+- group labels/descriptions and listbox accessibility labels;
+- Aurora Glass, Neon Voltage, and Raw Grid labels/descriptions;
+- custom-theme selection placeholders currently hard-coded in English;
+- native conversion, legacy best-effort, and failure warnings;
+- any new empty/error text introduced by the implementation.
+
+A translation-completeness test must compare every locale shape to English and reject missing keys.
+
+## Testing strategy
+
+### TDD requirement
+
+Each production behavior starts with a failing test. Tests must demonstrate failure before implementation and pass afterward.
+
+### Rust unit and fixture tests
+
+Create small deterministic fixtures for every convertible extension. Prefer generated fixtures in test helpers where practical; commit binary fixtures only when generation would no longer test a real parser path.
+
+Cover:
+
+- extension and signature dispatch;
+- successful conversion for DOC, DOCX, PDF, HTML, XLS, XLSX, XLM, PPTX, ODT, ODP, ODS, and RTF;
+- headings, paragraphs, lists, links, tables, Unicode, entities, and line breaks;
+- slide and sheet ordering;
+- malformed/truncated containers;
+- empty/image-only content;
+- legacy quality classification;
+- disabled conversion;
+- cache hit/miss and invalidation;
+- cached quality metadata;
+- no panic across malformed fixtures;
+- no Tauri Node process, sidecar, `externalBin`, or bundled runtime.
+
+### UI tests
+
+Cover:
+
+- at most three theme group cards;
+- built-in options live inside Themes rather than separate cards;
+- Pet themes behavior remains intact;
+- custom group visibility and activation;
+- keyboard and ARIA behavior;
+- new IDs normalize and persist;
+- old `glass` settings resolve to Aurora Glass;
+- translation completeness across nine locales;
+- no hard-coded new English strings in `ThemeStylePicker`;
+- Tabs/Focus header parity selectors for four requested themes;
+- Tokyo Night header gap for sidebar and TOC;
+- swatch/token presence for Aurora Glass, Neon Voltage, and Raw Grid.
+
+### Variant regression checks
+
+- Electron conversion tests remain green with `@the-long-ride/markdown-them`.
+- VS Code conversion tests remain green with `@the-long-ride/markdown-them`.
+- Chromium/web capability tests remain unchanged unless shared type additions require updates.
+- Tauri builds and tests on Windows GNU/MSVC as configured, Linux, and macOS where CI supports them.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+1. Tauri converts all currently supported document extensions without spawning a child process.
+2. Tauri package/config/source contains no Node runtime, sidecar, runtime download, or document-conversion telemetry.
+3. Legacy DOC/XLS/XLM output is visibly marked best-effort in every supported language.
+4. Electron and VS Code retain working Markdown Them conversion.
+5. Settings shows no more than Themes, Pet themes, and Your custom themes.
+6. Aurora Glass replaces Evolved Glass under the compatible `glass` ID.
+7. Neon Voltage and Raw Grid are selectable, persistent, localized, and fully styled.
+8. Requested Tabs headers visually match Focus headers.
+9. Tokyo Night sidebar and TOC have the requested header gap without layout regressions.
+10. New implementation is covered by focused Rust, UI, localization, and cross-variant regression tests.
+11. Full lint/type/test/build commands available in the repository pass before completion, or any environment blocker is reported precisely.
+12. Final delivery is one cumulative binary-safe `.patch` against `markdown-explorer-2026-07-28-005234.zip`.
+
+## Source notes
+
+- `@the-long-ride/markdown-them@1.3.1` resolves in the uploaded lockfile to Mammoth, PDF2MD, JSZip, Fast XML Parser, OfficeParser, and Turndown.
+- The approved Rust replacement intentionally reproduces user-facing conversion outcomes, not internal JavaScript implementation details.
+- The uploaded archive has no `.git` metadata, so this design document cannot be committed in the extracted workspace. It will be included in the final patch.
